         <item>
          <widget class="LineEdit" name="txt_output_dir">
           <property name="minimumSize">
            <size>
             <width>0</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="maximumSize">
            <size>
             <width>16777215</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Where the baked lightmaps are written (optional).

Empty — the project's sourceimages folder.
Relative (e.g. 'lightmaps' or 'bake/lm') — resolved under sourceimages, so the path stays portable across projects.
Absolute (e.g. 'D:/bakes') — used as-is.

The folder is created if it doesn't exist. Browsing to a folder inside sourceimages stores it as a relative path. The image button saves each map beside its material's texture maps instead; this folder then takes only the objects whose material has none.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="placeholderText">
            <string>sourceimages</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item>
          <widget class="LineEdit" name="txt000">
           <property name="minimumSize">
            <size>
             <width>0</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="maximumSize">
            <size>
             <width>16777215</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Name affix for the baked lightmap (file + shader). A leading '_' (e.g. '_Lightmap') is treated as a suffix → &amp;lt;object&amp;gt;_Lightmap; a trailing '_' (e.g. 'LM_') as a prefix. Empty uses the placeholder default.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The button beside the field cycles Auto / Suffix / Prefix.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="placeholderText">
            <string>_Lightmap</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
        </layout>
       </widget>
      </item>
