           <property name="minimumSize">
            <size>
             <width>0</width>
             <height>30</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="maximumSize">
            <size>
             <width>16777215</width>
             <height>30</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Bake a lightmap for every object in Scope (minus the Exclude set) and wire it for the engine: pack lightmap UVs, Arnold-bake white-card lighting into them, dilate the seams, denoise, then record it on the mesh. The material and its texture UVs are untouched — the engine composites albedo × lightmap.

   Re-baking replaces the previous maps; Revert to Source (header menu) removes the wiring.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="text">
            <string>Bake Lightmaps</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
